# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in; every make target exports these.
# Keep in sync with backend/internal/config/config.go.

# Encrypts the provider API keys and the users' two-step login secrets stored
# in the database: base64 of 32 random bytes. make dev / make dev-backend generate one into .env if it is empty.
SECRET_KEY=

# SQLite database file. The make targets run the backend from backend/, so
# this path is relative to backend/ (the file ends up in backend/gelirgider.db).
DB_PATH=./gelirgider.db

# Port the backend listens on. The vite dev server proxies /api to it, so
# changing it here moves both ends together.
# PORT=8080

# Address the backend binds to. Empty, the default, binds every interface,
# which the Docker image needs; make dev and make dev-backend set 127.0.0.1,
# so the plain-http dev backend is not reachable from the LAN.
# HOST=

# Mark the session cookie Secure, and read the client IP from X-Forwarded-For.
# Only the literal value true enables them; leave them off for plain-http
# local development.
# COOKIE_SECURE=false
# TRUST_PROXY=false

# With TRUST_PROXY=true: how many reverse proxies sit in front of the backend.
# Each must append the address it saw to X-Forwarded-For (nginx's
# $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for, Traefik, Caddy with trusted_proxies), or, as the
# outermost, replace it; the backend takes the entry this many places from
# the right and ignores the client-supplied ones left of it. Too high a value
# lets a client pick its own IP for rate limiting; too low makes every client
# share a proxy's address. Ignored when TRUST_PROXY is off.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# API_DOCS_DIR is not set here: make dev and make dev-backend set it to
# apidocs for the backend, which serves the API docs at /api/docs/ only when
# it is set (ADR 0013). With COOKIE_SECURE=true the backend ignores it and
# serves no API docs.
